* Rail-to-rail op-amp model of the sensor_frontend example.
* Written for cuprite_wire and released under its license (MIT).
*
* Single pole: open-loop gain 100k, pole at 10 Hz (gain-bandwidth 1 MHz).
* The output swings to within 10 mV of the supply rails, with 50 ohm output
* resistance; the supply draws 100 uA. The internal node is clamped near the
* rails so that the output recovers quickly from clipping.
.subckt rrio_opamp inp inn vcc vee out
Rin inp inn 10Meg
G1 0 n1 inp inn 1m
R1 n1 0 100Meg
C1 n1 0 159p
D1 n1 vcc dclamp
D2 vee n1 dclamp
Bout n2 0 V = min(max(V(n1), V(vee) + 0.01), V(vcc) - 0.01)
Rout n2 out 50
Iq vcc vee 100u
.model dclamp D(IS=1e-14)
.ends rrio_opamp
